Z||000000||SloPonti||09-01-99||04:19 PM||||when i stop my car at a stop light i get a vibration that will rattle the dash and steering wheel-it is only when the car is at a complete stop-and when i put my car in neutral or park the vibration goes away!  i wondered if it was the dog bone so i replaced it with a cheap one from autozone about a year ago and that did not fix it?  do i need the good dog bone from the fiero store?  the car idles about 850-900 rpms when at idle and in gear-when put into park the car idles at about 1000rpms!  any help would be greatly appreciated!!<br>
Z||000001||theogre||09-01-99||07:07 PM||||what motor is it?<p>you shure the motor isn't up against something? the motor end of the 4cyl dog bone is slotted for a reason.....<p>That "cheap" bone is likely the same as the stock one. Try replacing the bushings with the urethane ones. ((BTW A stock 4 cyl bone can allow up to 2 inches of engine travel.))
Z||000002||SloPonti||09-02-99||03:34 PM||||the motor is a 4-banger but i am not sure what you mean by the motor being up against something??  the motor sits in the middle of the trunk and is clear of everything.  also when i put the dog bone in i tightened both bolts up tight.  is one end supposed to be loose to allow for movement?? thanks
Z||000003||Dale||09-02-99||07:44 PM||||check your fluid level in your trany.  It sounds like the trany is trying to engage early.  At worst the clutches could be worn.  How many miles on it?  Is it a very fast vibration like a palm sander or a slower chugging vibration?  Those are my technical words for the day.
